; 05-wrapping-arithmetic.l0 -- add, sub, and mul wrap silently (spec 3),
; and nothing reports that they did. This type checks and prints
; 0 and -9223372036854775808: 2^32 * 2^32 and (2^63 - 1) + 1, both wrong,
; with nothing to say so.
;
; What an exact calculator has to write instead is ../calc/rat.l0's c_add,
; c_mul, o_add, o_mul, both, and times10 (about 45 of its 174 lines,
; nearly all of 18 to 70 and 127 to 140), and every rational operation
; then threads an Option through each product. Even so, Knuth's addition
; (a*(d/g) + c*(b/g)) can overflow in its numerator while the reduced
; answer fits: 97 of 100,000 random lines (../data/exprs.txt) are reported
; as overflows that Python answers in 64 bits. A widening multiply or a
; checked builtin would remove both costs.
(def main () int
  (let a (write_line (digits (mul 4294967296 4294967296)))
    (let b (write_line (digits (add 9223372036854775807 1)))
      0)))
